On Mon, May 2, 2011 at 2:05 AM, Ian Johnson <blindbravado@gmail.com> wrote:
> Shouldn't you not do that anyway, since {lo} is distributive?

"lo" (at least in xorlo, which is what we were talking about) is in
itself neither distributive nor non-distributive.

The definition is:

  lo broda = zo'e noi ke'a broda

and there is obviously no requirement for "zo'e" to be distribitive
(or non-distributive).

mu'o mi'e xorxes

